 {"id": "agent-chat-close-lifecycle",
  "acceptance": "Closing a chat is accepted at once in every stage of its turn or of a display repair (streaming, provider retry, silent, reconnecting, degraded, paused, exhausted, an acknowledgement pending, an approval waiting, the runtime exited, completed): the repair stops, a receipt or retry that lands later attaches nothing, and no turn, approval answer or second close is sent. A prepared empty chat closes without an error; a close before the first display snapshot detaches the late subscription; a close during preparation lets no late startup dispatch; queued input is sealed and late receipts or completions change nothing; a sibling chat is unaffected and a close that was not confirmed keeps the tab for a retry.",
